ring some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/83/8306880f3f6b3d936d1e690cf75eb9e1a999f5b1c914d10c1886296317664fbe.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "086a8eea-bc9f-5aea-bf4b-1d01099fd0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564847} {:answer/id #uuid "74050f25-2cd5-55cc-a4e6-84f22bf022aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "086a8eea-bc9f-5aea-bf4b-1d01099fd0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564847} :answer-field/id #uuid "be694608-819a-50b8-a937-c2edbf666555" :answer-field/key "At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564902} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32847a7b-e2d8-5638-948f-cfb5df50edb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564863} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb2dc10-42a7-51a9-b990-f7f7acdc709f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32847a7b-e2d8-5638-948f-cfb5df50edb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564863} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdb2b7b1-7760-5b0f-b38a-f35653132354" :answer-field/key "At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564909} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3701ee33-5daf-549f-b8a4-6a86bbcd3b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564866} {:answer/id #uuid "c407bb4f-db56-595d-bc0e-5878c3a4d5a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c407bb4f-db56-595d-bc0e-5878c3a4d5a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564906} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8bc7d29-c85d-552e-8bc7-b184038b82c9" :answer-field/key "At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "26112629-51c5-582f-837e-44806c4fa45a" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIn an open quadrant, each squared coordinate is positive, so the remaining coordinate factors and coefficient determine the sign.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/6e/6ec462e2ce1055ca352de84813bc6d72731d74f93d44a1513b1dc284b504cb0b.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative”; “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab5e8ff6-47e3-5907-9288-b65fe7ad32e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564894} {:answer/id #uuid "d440eaba-5164-5dde-9119-92957d8c698e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d440eaba-5164-5dde-9119-92957d8c698e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564911} :answer-field/id #uuid "806fd6b0-987f-51dc-b969-151cc4e0da9c" :answer-field/key "At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1384760f-c94a-5c81-a693-b7997a8928c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564853} {:answer/id #uuid "9f1b31d4-09b2-5250-bb35-b48863ba5adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f1b31d4-09b2-5250-bb35-b48863ba5adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564892} :answer-field/id #uuid "d95da847-52a7-5894-8d50-6079fe0472a1" :answer-field/key "At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #e